DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TimelinePage shipped at web parity: a pure @Observable TimelinePageModel (ADR-004 — no
networking in the view) bound through an injected TimelineDataSource seam (useVehicles + the two inline state queries),
resolving the loading / empty / error / success phases; the four summary metric cards; the proportional
state-distribution bar with the full eight-state legend; the stacked daily-breakdown BarChart on the P3 Swift Charts
wrapper; and the five-column state-transitions table on the shared TSDataTable. Adaptive across macOS/iPad/iPhone (the
header + metric grid reflow on compact width). Durations stay SI seconds in the model and format to h/m/s only at the
render boundary; every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; the page is
deep-linkable via the new .timeline route. Verified by all 8 sources compiling in the real macOS app target with ZERO
diagnostics (against the real components + Shared.xcframework), an executed Swift-6 logic harness (30/30), and clean
swiftformat / swiftlint --strict / placeholder gates. The only RED is one pre-existing out-of-scope Driving-sibling
error (forbidden to commit-fix) plus shared-sandbox OOM contention.

